<span id="A2.T5.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">18.03 Differential Equations</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T5.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:199.2pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Find general solutions of the differential equations. If an initial condition is given, find the corresponding particular solution. Throughout, primes denote derivatives with respect to <math id="A2.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}+y=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}+y=2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T5.2.4.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:128.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.2.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(x)=2(1-e^{-x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(x)=2(1-e^{-x})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
