<span id="A2.T5.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">18.06 Linear Algebra</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T5.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T5.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:199.2pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.2.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Find a combination <math id="A2.T5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}w_{1}+x_{2}w_{2}+x_{3}w_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}w_{1}+x_{2}w_{2}+x_{3}w_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> that gives the zero vector with <math id="A2.T5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.T5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the vector <math id="A2.T5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1;2;3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1;2;3)</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.T5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the vector <math id="A2.T5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4;5;6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4;5;6)</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.T5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is the vector <math id="A2.T5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(7;8;9)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(7;8;9)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></td>
